{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Lynyrd Skynyrd hits collection and Tom Petty retrospective feel like natural next choices because I have repeatedly chosen older songs gathered into artist collections and compilations.",
    "The Nightfly appeals to the melodic, softer side of my listening, which also draws me to Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The heavier progressive rock and metal choices miss what I want today: familiar melodies and approachable songs. Sharing a broad rock connection is not enough.",
    "Blunderbuss feels more like an album to explore than a familiar collection to revisit, while Crazy Ex-Girlfriend and Fever do not give me a clear enough connection to my listening to choose them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in classic rock seems to have been stretched into an interest in much heavier music.",
    "Choosing some individual albums seems to have been taken as a stronger invitation to explore than my repeated return to best-of collections suggests."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The recurring greatest-hits and compilation titles matter because I am often looking for familiar songs rather than a whole unfamiliar album.",
    "Melody and a gentler sound matter alongside older rock connections. If Animals is the Pink Floyd album, it interests me, but the hits collections are still stronger choices today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly capture my interest in older rock but miss how strongly familiar collections and melodic songs guide my choices right now."
}"}
